  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID&apos;s Youth are Resilient, Interconnected, Socially Cohesive and Engaged (YouthRISE) Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  Youth are Resilient, Interconnected, Socially Cohesive and Engaged (YouthRISE) activity addresses social cohesion issues stemming from the influx of Rohingya refugees in Cox&apos;s Bazar area. This activity supports young people in the host communities to become more resilient to impacts of conflict, more capable of frequently resolving local conflicts in their community in peaceful and non-violent ways, and less likely to be involved in violence. YouthRISE will help host community youth build resilience by ensuring that underlying economic grievances are addressed, strengthening their skills for constructive engagement, and addressing harmful gender norms. With FY 2022 funds, USAID will enhance the capacity of local youth, with the goal of developing social and economic resilience in host communities.  USAID will provide livelihood training to 1,200 youth coupled with life/leadership skills to help address conflict in their communities. With FY 2022 funds, this activity will also engage youth in the informal justice system, and involve 3,000 youth in events, training, and activities designed to build mass support for peace and reconciliation.This activity is in line with the Integrated Country Strategy (ICS) Mission Goals One and the U.S. government development objective of strengthened resilience to shocks and stressors. This activity will contribute towards meeting the Rohingya refugee ($1.8m) earmark.</narrative>
  </description>
